  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "[Version 0.3.0]\n\nThis version introduces a new framework which is not compatible to the previous version.\nIt relies more on interfaces rather than abstract classes to describe symbols.\nMeanwhile, previous extension methods to 'ILGenerator' have been removed,\nfor they can be replaced by extension methods to 'ISymbol<T>' with more convenient usage.\n\nCompared to 0.2.x versions, this new framework has full support for non-generic symbols;\nnow all non-generic symbols can be converted to generic symbols, \nand most extension methods can be invoked on them.\n\nWe also implement unit tests for all core features of this framework to ensure its correctness;\nand we have been doing dog-fooding to improve the design of this framework on several projects,\nincluding but not limited to InjectionExpert and SnapshotExpert.\n\nNOTE:\n\nThe Roslyn Compiler of .NET 10 has some issues causing it to generate false-positive warnings\nabout the nullability constraints of generic extension methods, such as CS8620.\nThis issue has been reported to Microsoft and we are following up with updates.",
